# synthetic-wirefault.jsonl — HAND-WRITTEN, not a wire capture.
#
# The two faults the transport synthesises itself, which no server ever sends
# and therefore no capture can hold:
#
#   * `client/protocolError` — `read_loop` raises it for a line it cannot
#     frame, for an error frame with a null id, and for a response no request
#     is waiting on. Every one of them used to fall into the fold's
#     untyped-method catch-all and vanish (finding `client-adapter-4`); it is
#     an error card of its own now.
#   * `client/gapAborted` — the backfill a `view/gap` promised gave up, either
#     because `view/page` failed or because the page loop or the parked-event
#     buffer hit its bound (finding `client-adapter-7`). The row withdraws the
#     promise the `view/gap` row made.
#
# A real `client/protocolError` carries no `sessionId` — a frame-level fault
# belongs to no session — and `SessionView::apply` files it against the view
# that is open. This file gives it one so the fold-level test has something to
# fold; the row it produces is identical either way.
#
# The `synthetic-` prefix is load-bearing: nothing here was ever on a wire.
